  <compounddef id="Demonstrating-example" kind="example">
    <compoundname>Demonstrating</compoundname>
    <briefdescription>
<para>No-op for arena allocators (individual deallocation not supported) </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>No-op for arena allocators (individual deallocation not supported)<parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>ptr</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Pointer to memory (ignored) </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>bytes</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Size of allocation (ignored) </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>alignment</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Alignment used (ignored)</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
Arena allocators do not support individual deallocation. All memory is freed together via reset() or when the arena is destroyed. This method is a no-op to maintain compatibility with the Allocator interface.</para>
<para>This design is intentional and provides:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Much faster allocation (no per-allocation metadata)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>No fragmentation</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Simpler implementation</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Better cache locality</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para><simplesect kind="note"><para>To free memory, use reset() to free all allocations, or restore() to rollback to a checkpoint, or let the arena be destroyed.</para>
</simplesect>
no-op behavior <programlisting><codeline><highlight class="keyword">auto</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>arena<sp/>=<sp/><ref refid="namespacecslt_1ad55f4168d9f1832627c6d75e60d14a6c" kindref="member">cslt::move</ref>(<ref refid="classcslt_1_1ArenaAllocator_1ab71e5fc5e1cf3e9b07ad7208465a7b0f" kindref="member">cslt::ArenaAllocator::Heap</ref>(4096).value());</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="keywordtype">void</highlight><highlight class="normal">*<sp/>ptr<sp/>=<sp/>arena-&gt;alloc(256).value();</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="keywordtype">size_t</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>size_before<sp/>=<sp/>arena-&gt;size();</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>This<sp/>does<sp/>nothing</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">arena-&gt;return_element(ptr,<sp/>256);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>Size<sp/>unchanged<sp/>-<sp/>memory<sp/>still<sp/>allocated</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">assert(arena-&gt;size()<sp/>==<sp/>size_before);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>To<sp/>actually<sp/>free<sp/>memory:</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">arena-&gt;reset();</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">assert(arena-&gt;size()<sp/>==<sp/>0);</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting> <programlisting filename="Demonstrating"></programlisting> </para>
